 jane foster has  managed to land a comeback in thor love  and thunder while darcy returned in one  division as a full-fledged doctor yet  darcy made no mention of ian the romance  and the character of ian altogether was  apparently just not meant to last very  long in this franchise  in the middle of captain america civil  war tony stark drops a bombshell on  steve rogers he and pepper potts are  taking a break after the character was  absent from avengers age of ultron due  to her duties to stark industries this  confirmed that stark was officially  single again thanks in part to his  non-stop adventures with the avengers it  was a significant development that also  helped explain why potts was suddenly  m.i.a from the franchise  pepper  we're taking a break but this  development was abruptly upended in  spider-man homecoming when pepper potts  not only reappeared but was being  intimate with stark as if nothing had  ever happened there was even a gag about  stark popping the question to potts in  lieu of introducing spider-man in his  iron spider outfit to members of the  press the sudden loss of pots in stark's  life never got referenced in the  following two avengers movies either  making this a strange unexplained detour  in the love life of two principal mcu  figures  in the wake of the avengers thor the  dark world fine scientist eric selvig  struggling to maintain a proper  psychological state having had loki  control his mind for an extended period  of time selvig is now fit to bouts of  strange behavior like wandering around  stonehenge naked he's even been locked  up in a psych ward which darcy and ian  must break him out of to assist thor in  his quest to defeat the dark elves the  lingering after effects of selvik  getting his brain scrambled in the  avengers wouldn't last forever when thor  went to recruit his help in age of  ultron selvig was seen walking out of a  college that he teaches at not only had  he returned to his regular day job but  he seemed to have fully recovered from  his encounter with loki  at the end of iron man 2 weapons  manufacturer justin hammer is arrested  by police officers as this happens he  calls back to pepper potts that it isn't  over with you i'm going to be seeing you  again real soon perhaps that was  originally the plan mcu films don't just  keep any villain alive and well after  all keeping hammer alive and thirsting  for vengeance had to be thought of as a  way to set up future installments  however for whatever reason hammer has  not reemerged in the mcu iron man 3 had  no place for hammer replacing him with  killian while other movies starring tony  stark like captain america civil war  also found no room for him the most  peculiar part of this is that rockwell's  profile has increased substantially  since iron man 2 came out having won a  best supporting actor academy award and  getting another oscar nomination in the  same category one would think marvel  studios would be scrambling to bring him  back instead rockwell's entire presence  in the franchise has been limited to  iron man 2 and a tiny cameo in the short  film all hail the king  in the incredible hulk viewers aren't  just introduced to the hulk they also  get a first glimpse of the franchise's  version of the romance between bruce  banner and betty ross this is a  relationship complicated by banner  watching out for his heart rate  quickening out of fear of turning into  the hulk this dynamic was established as  a crucial part of banner's life and was  even used as a signifier that there may  be more of banner in the hulk than their  appear however betty has never  resurfaced in the mcu despite her father  general thunderbolt ross managing to  re-emerge as a recurring presence in  recent entries in the saga the character  hasn't even been referenced again either  by her father or by banner instead  banner took up a romance with black  widow in avengers age of ultron which  seemed to close the book on this initial  love affair for the hulk's alter ego the  only post-incredible hulk nod to the  character in the mcu was through the  initial code name of the hulkbuster  armor ai in age of ultron being veronica  a nod towards the archie comics  character of the same name who had a  rivalry with a lady named betty  captain america the winter soldier ends  with a genuinely interesting beat after  faking his death earlier in the film one  would expect fury to just return to his  regular day-to-day duties by the end of  the feature instead fury makes the  conscious choice to remain deceased to  the general public the viewer even gets  a glimpse at his headstone in washington  dc cemetery as fury walks off screen in  the winter soldier the possibilities for  what he could be up to next are  limitless strangely then age of ultron  brings things right back to the original  status quo while initially fury is  depicted as someone who's been off the  grid for a while he's eventually shown  to be manning a helicarrier in his  traditional leather garb to help  sokovian civilians get to safety rather  than a shadowy individual believed to be  dead by most fury is once again a public  figure that everyone knows is alive and  well it's a strange move that undercuts  the ending of the winter soldier and all  the narrative possibilities that fury  remaining dead could have brought  in the initial guardians of the galaxy  movie xandar is an important planet it's  where four of the five titular  superheroes meet up as well as home to  the headquarters of the nova corps  organization and the backdrop for ronin  the accuser's massive final battle to  execute his vengeance against the  planet's occupants given all that and  the fact that it housed an infinity  stone at the end of guardians of the  galaxy fans might expect such a location  and its characters including nova prime  and roman day to reappear throughout  future mcu adventures particularly  cosmic-based ones instead the planet  hasn't reappeared at all in subsequent  films the nova corps gets name dropped  in guardians of the galaxy vol 2 while  zandar also gets mentioned in thor  ragnarok and avengers infinity war  that's the extent that this planet is  factored into the franchise post  guardians of the galaxy with even its  destruction by thanos happening entirely  off screen zandar started as a seemingly  important place but it's largely brushed  aside in the mythology of the marvel  cinematic universe  starting with the show's second season  bobby morse was a critical part of  agents of shield and its ever-expanding  mythology however she and her love  interest lance hunter eventually left  shield in the third season episode  parting shot in universe they were  forced to leave to keep coulson and  company safe however beyond these  fictitious confines morse's sudden  absence was done to allow herself and  hunter to headline a spin-off show  entitled marvel's most wanted they're  not coming back  they've been disavowed what are you  talking about there were no good options  however those plans hit a snag when abc  opted to pass on most wanted leaving the  two characters in a state of limbo  though hunter managed to return in a  guest appearance capacity in a later  episode of shield morse remained m.i.a  for the rest of the program's run part  of this appears to be due to scheduling  conflicts for actress adrian pilicki who  eventually found a lead role on the fox  sci-fi series the orville however no  official reason has ever been given for  her sudden departure whatever caused the  character's absence a whole was left in  the agents of shield mythology that kept  all storylines related to morse  awkwardly unresolved  for ant-man and the wasp the two titular  tiny heroes faced off not against thanos  or he who remains or ultron but rather  ghost a woman who can move through  objects and constantly looks like she's  glitching in and out of reality ghost  turned out to be a morally complicated  figure one who merely wanted to cure her  condition not to destroy the world while  she wasn't above doing bad things she  was also somebody whose life wasn't  defined by acts of malice a scene at the  end of ant-man and the wasp suggested  that she and her surrogate father figure  bill foster would be sticking together  for whatever came next but ghost has  ended up being absent so far from the  rest of the marvel cinematic universe  despite ant-man even name-dropping her  during the mid-credits scene of ant-man  and the wasp ghost has never appeared in  another mcu entry it also doesn't look  like ghosts will get her storyline  resolved in the upcoming ant-man and the  wasp quantomania either there's been no  news on ghost star hannah john kramen  getting cast in that film plus she's  committed to starring in red sonja  in the middle of spider-man homecoming  the young web crawler's inexperience  with properly handling criminals is made  apparent through the bungling of his  attempt to stop a weapons sale on a  ferry this transaction involves the  henchmen of the film's primary villain  adrian toomes aka the vulture but it  also entails matt gargan a criminal who  in the comics is also known as the super  villain the scorpion here gargan is  depicted as just a regular person albeit  one with a scorpion tattoo on his neck  he quickly vanishes in the chaos of  spider-man's botched attempt to stop the  crime the mid-credit scene of homecoming  in which a battered and vengeful gargan  confronts tombs in prison and asks if he  knows the secret identity of spider-man  seemed to be setting up the idea of  scorpion as a recurring threat to  spider-man however gargan has made no  further appearances in either spider-man  far from home or other sony marvel  productions like venom there's also been  no word on him appearing in future  productions like spider-man no way home  while a rumored presence in the future  silver and black went nowhere once that  film got canned in pre-production while  gargan was useful in showcasing spidey's  inexperience in homecoming the seeming  lack of interest in further exploring  the character indicates his usefulness  in the mcu may have come to a close  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite marvel movies are coming  soon subscribe to our youtube channel  and hit the bell so you don't miss a  single one

